Inside the supermarket, I go directly to the meat counter.
Only a few people are waiting there.
It is my turn quickly.
The butcher smiles at me.
"Good day, what can I do for you?" he asks.
"Good day," I answer.
"I need mixed minced meat, please."
"Gladly."
"How much would you like?"
"Exactly half a kilo, please," I say.
He takes the minced meat and puts it on the scale.
"That is five hundred and ten grams," he says.
"Is that also okay with you?"
"Yes, that is perfect," I answer.
He wraps the meat in paper.
Then he hands me the package over the glass counter.
"Here you go."
"Do you need anything else?"
"No, thank you, that is all."
"Then I wish you a nice day!" the butcher says.
"Thank you, you too!" I call out and walk on.
